"""
Tests whether SeqNetMut's performance and biological output are specific to
the curated breast-cancer seed set, or reproducible with any degree-matched
random gene set of the same size.

For each of N_PERM permutations:
  1. Sample 71 random genes degree-matched to the 71 real training seeds
  2. Recompute RWR and max_seq from the permuted seeds (mut is unchanged)
  3. Measure CV AUPR (seed-recovery performance)
  4. Score genome-wide, take top-100 candidates
  5. Build induced subgraph of top-100, run Leiden, record modularity Q
  6. Record overlap with the REAL top-100 candidate list

Outputs empirical two-sided p-values for CV AUPR and modularity, plus the
distribution of top-100 overlap under the null.


"""
